+## Troubleshooting
+
+**The sign-in tab spins forever after login.** Chromium passes
+`https://www.google.com/` as the `continue` URL. The post-login page only links
+to targets on this service's own origin, so the tab is safe to close - the
+DICE header was already processed and the account is signed in. If you mapped
+the Google hostnames in the hosts file but do not listen on 443 with TLS, any
+navigation to those hostnames hangs until it times out.
+
+**The `sync` token says "Token was revoked".** Chromium is still using the
+default sync URL (`clients4.google.com`). Regenerate `gaia-config.json` (it now
+contains `sync_url`) or start the client with
+`--sync-url=http://<host>:<port>`.
+
+**Sign-in is disabled / "Not Consented for Sync".** Sign-in being disabled
+means the OAuth client is not configured - use the `api_keys` block from
+`gen-gaia-config`. "Not Consented for Sync" just means the sync toggle is off;
+enable it in `afree://settings/syncSetup`.
+
+**Nothing shows up in the sync tables.** Start the service with
+`--log-level debug` and watch for `sync: get updates` / `sync: commit`; then
+check `afree://sync-internals` for the sync URL and the last error.
+
 ## Roadmap
 
 1. Sync invalidations (push) instead of polling; conflict detection.
diff --git a/tools/afree-login-service/src/gaia.mjs b/tools/afree-login-service/src/gaia.mjs
index 7bb1f208ec..d84d1a9406 100644
--- a/tools/afree-login-service/src/gaia.mjs
+++ b/tools/afree-login-service/src/gaia.mjs
@@ -334,9 +334,26 @@ export class GaiaService {
     return url.toString();
   }
 
+  /**
+   * Returns true when `url` is on this service's own origin. Only same-origin
+   * targets are offered as links on the post-login page: Chromium passes the
+   * Google base URL as `continue`, which is unreachable in a self-hosted or
+   * hosts-mapped deployment and would leave the tab hanging.
+   * @param {string | null} url
+   */
+  isSameOrigin(url) {
+    if (!url) {
+      return false;
+    }
+    try {
+      return new URL(url).origin === this.config.publicUrl;
+    } catch {
+      return false;
+    }
+  }
+
   /** @param {import('node:http').IncomingMessage} req */
-  clientInfo(req) {
-    return {
+  clientInfo(req) {    return {
       ip: req.socket.remoteAddress ?? '',
       userAgent: String(req.headers['user-agent'] ?? ''),
     };
@@ -764,7 +781,7 @@ export class GaiaService {
         renderSignedInPage({
           email: user.display_email,
           gaiaId: user.gaia_id,
-          continueUrl: target ?? '',
+          continueUrl: this.isSameOrigin(target) ? target ?? '' : '',
         }),
         headers,
     );
@@ -1234,7 +1251,9 @@ export class GaiaService {
